### 1.2 **Version Chain and Leaf Node Definition**

Leaf nodes maintain a version chain for MVCC. These chains must support lock-free updates and point-in-time visibility based on transaction timestamps.

```cpp
struct Version {
    uint64_t commit_ts;
    uint64_t value;
    std::atomic<Version*> next;

    Version(uint64_t ts, uint64_t val, Version* next_ver = nullptr)
        : commit_ts(ts), value(val), next(next_ver) {}
};

struct LeafNode : public BaseNode {
    std::atomic<Version*> version_chain;

    LeafNode() : version_chain(nullptr) {}

    void add_version(uint64_t ts, uint64_t value) {
        Version* new_version = new Version(ts, value);
        Version* head = version_chain.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
        do {
            new_version->next = head;
        } while (!version_chain.compare_exchange_weak(head, new_version, 
                std::memory_order_release, std::memory_order_acquire));
    }
};
